{"availability":"available","full":"relm-us/svelt-yjs","name":"svelt-yjs","description":"A library for your Svelte app that lets you build Svelte stores from Yjs types.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Svelte","stars":95,"forks":6,"created":"2020-10-16T14:45:14Z","updated":"2024-01-12T16:59:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://svelt-yjs.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:38:44.435Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T22:38:44.435Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T22:38:44.435Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:59:11.992Z","stars":95,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-11T20:53:29.501Z","stars":95,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-17T22:38:44.435Z","stars":95,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Svelte"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Svelt-yjs is a library for your Svelte app that lets you build Svelte stores from Yjs types. When built on the client-side Yjs library, your Svelte app gets transport-agnostic synchronization (e.g. y-webrtc, y-websocket ) across networks and undo/redo management basically for free.","Yjs is often thought of as a way to make collaborative text editing work in a browser, but its underlying technology is amenable to a variety of web use cases. We think Svelte and Yjs are positioned to make collaborative, local-first apps much easier to build.","At Relm, for example, we've been using it as the synchronization layer between participants in a collaborative 3D world."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/relm-us/svelt-yjs/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dd94cf2cf8fdc0503bb75183d7c62fa915f91da710225ff6dd8f49b89edeb6e4","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.147Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T20:53:29.648Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Svelt-yjs is a library for your Svelte app that lets you build Svelte stores from Yjs types. When built on the client-side Yjs library, your Svelte app gets transport-agnostic synchronization (e.g. y-we